(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-10"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-10","label":"2026 年 9 月 10 日","date":"2026-09-10","range":"","theme":"社论","themes":["社论"],"sources":["Economist"],"title":"Anti-social","titleZh":"反社会的","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":10,"vocab":30,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.10精读.pdf","headline":{"title":"Anti-social","titleZh":"反社会的","source":"Economist","series":"考研那些事儿之社论系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"It seemed A parent’s dream. To manage the time her 14‑year‑old son spent online, Harini Naidu had tried various tactics: from restricting Wi‑Fi access to turning the internet off at night. So she was excited when Australia became the first country in the world to ban social‑media accounts for under‑16s. But the rules, imposed in December, “literally did nothing”. Her son lost his YouTube account, but can still watch videos without logging in. Ms Naidu’s daughter Ishana was 15, but has kept her accounts on X, Instagram, Snapchat and TikTok. Ishana says: “It’s so underwhelming that people have forgotten there’s a ban.” They do not even have to hide behind virtual private networks.","zh":"这本来似乎是每个家长梦寐以求的结果。为了控制14岁儿子上网的时间，哈里尼·奈杜尝试过各种办法：从限制Wi-Fi接入，到晚上直接断网。因此，当澳大利亚成为全球第一个禁止16岁以下未成年人注册社交媒体账号的国家时，她十分兴奋。然而，这项于去年12月实施的规定“简直什么作用都没起”。她的儿子失去了YouTube账号，却依然可以不登录就观看视频。奈杜女士的女儿伊莎娜当时15岁，但她在X、Instagram、Snapchat和TikTok上的账号都保住了。伊莎娜说：“效果实在太差了，差到人们都已经忘了还有这么一项禁令。”他们甚至都不需要借助虚拟私人网络（VPN）来掩人耳目。"},{"index":2,"en":"The experiences of teens like Ishana matter to other countries, too. Since Australia brought in its curbs, dozens have done the same, or are considering it. On August 24th New Zealand announced a planned ban. Policymakers worry that social media cause various harms to the young. They also know that bans are popular with adults. Many cheered on August 26th when Meta agreed to change its products for under‑18s in most American states, including a two‑hours‑per‑day limit on their scrolling, after settling a lawsuit alleging its platforms harm youngsters.","zh":"像伊莎娜这样的青少年的经历，对其他国家同样具有参考意义。自澳大利亚实施相关限制措施以来，已有数十个国家效仿或者正在考虑这样做。8月24日，新西兰宣布计划实施禁令。政策制定者担心，社交媒体会对年轻人造成各种伤害。他们也知道，禁令很受成年人欢迎。8月26日，当Meta同意在美国大多数州调整其面向18岁以下人群的产品后，许多成年人对此拍手叫好。调整措施包括将每天的刷屏时间限制在两小时以内。此前，Meta刚刚就一桩指控其平台伤害未成年人的诉讼达成和解。"},{"index":3,"en":"Yet so far, Australia’s policy has proved largely ineffective. At first the government was able to tout some successes. Social‑media platforms had removed, restricted or deactivated almost 5m accounts in the first month. And it may be too early to write off the effectiveness of Australia’s new rules. But studies have shown they have so far had minimal impact on usage. One in the British Medical Journal in June found that, three months after restrictions were introduced, 85% of under‑16s said they still used banned platforms. Twelve‑ and 13‑year‑olds spent the same amount of time on social media as before the ban. Worries that children migrate to alternative platforms, with lower safety standards, were mostly unfounded—but largely because so many remain on existing ones.","zh":"方案。然而，到目前为止，澳大利亚的这项政策基本上收效甚微。起初，政府还能够拿出一些成果来宣传。实施禁令后的第一个月，社交媒体平台就删除、限制使用或停用了近500万个账号。况且，现在断言澳大利亚新规没有效果或许还为时过早。但研究表明，到目前为止，这些规定对社交媒体使用情况的影响微乎其微。《英国医学杂志》6月发表的一项研究发现，在限制措施实施三个月后，85%的16岁以下青少年表示，他们仍在使用被禁的社交媒体平台。12岁和13岁的孩子花在社交媒体上的时间与禁令实施前一样多。人们原本担心孩子会选择安全标准更低的其他媒体平台，但事实证明这种担忧大多没有成为现实——不过，这主要是因为许多的孩子仍然选择原有平台。"},{"index":4,"en":"Young Aussies are keen to stay online. Some spy a challenge, says Ishana, as under‑16s “want to use social media more because it’s banned”. The young “know how to outsmart the system”, she explains, including by creating joint accounts with friends, which she thinks confuses age‑checking systems. Yet she says several accounts with her real date of birth were not removed. Many under‑16s have made new accounts using a fake age. Others have entered their parents’ or siblings’ details. t/ To gain an advantage over","zh":"合作。澳大利亚的年轻人仍然很想继续上网。伊莎娜说，一些未成年人甚至把这当成了一种挑战，因为16岁以下的孩子“反而因为社交媒体被禁止使用而更想用”。她解释说，年轻人“知道怎么钻系统的空子”，比如和朋友创建共同账号，她认为这种做法会让年龄验证系统难以判断。不过，她说，有几个使用真实出生日期注册的账号却没有被删除。许多16岁以下的孩子用虚假的年龄信息创建了新账号。还有一些人则填写了父母或兄弟姐妹的信息。"},{"index":5,"en":"Some blame tech firms for not enforcing the rules. KJR, a software‑testing company, recently opened 50 social‑media accounts in Australia claiming the user to be 16. It said only one site did any verification and all 50 accounts remained active. The government is trying to beef up its rules, including by doubling fines on offending firms","zh":"一些人将责任归咎于科技公司没有落实这些规定。软件测试公司KJR最近在澳大利亚开设了50个社交媒体账号，并声称这些账号的用户年龄均为16岁。该公司表示，只有一个网站进行了身份验证，而这50个账号全部仍处于正常使用状态。澳大利亚政府正试图进一步强化相关规定，其中包括将违规企业的罚款金额提高一倍，增至9900万澳元（约合7100万美元）。政府还希望赋予澳大利亚电子安全专员更大的权力，要求社交媒体公司提供其平台的内部使用数据。"},{"index":6,"en":"Others blame the policy’s ineffectiveness so far partly on the technology meant to enforce it. Firms are using various tools, including AI, to analyse posts and scan faces. But facial‑age estimation software is not very accurate in distinguishing between, say, a 15‑ and 16‑year‑old. Lucina, a 15‑year‑old from the state of Victoria, says her face was scanned on Snapchat and she was told she looked 18. “The policy hasn’t been tested because it’s been technically impossible to enforce,” says Tama Leaver of Curtin University in Perth.","zh":"还有一些人认为，这项政策之所以迄今收效甚微，部分原因在于用于执行该政策的技术本身存在局限。社交媒体公司正在使用各种工具，包括人工智能，来分析帖子内容和扫描人脸。但用于估算年龄的面部识别软件，在区分比如15岁和16岁的用户时，并不十分准确。来自维多利亚州的15岁女孩露西娜说，Snapchat曾扫描过她的脸，随后却告诉她，她看起来已经18岁了。珀斯科廷大学的塔马·利弗说：“这项政策实际上并没有经过真正的检验，因为从技术层面来看，它根本无法得到有效执行。”"},{"index":7,"en":"concluding that the “only way to do this is to require people’s real IDs”—ie, an official digital or physical identity card—when they sign up to social media. Malaysia, one of just a few other countries where Australian‑style restrictions are in force, has opted for this method. L.S. Leonard, the chief legal counsel of Malaysia’s Communications and Multimedia Commission, the regulator, says that its assessment indicated that this would be “much more accurate” than the age‑assurance approach used in Australia.","zh":"利弗先生认为，其他正在计划制定类似法律的国家正在得出这样的结论：“要做到这一点，唯一的办法就是要求人们提供真实的身份证明”——也就是说，用户注册社交媒体账号时必须提供官方的数字或实体身份证件。马来西亚是少数几个已经实施类似澳大利亚限制措施的国家之一，该国选择了这种做法。马来西亚通信与多媒体委员会这一监管机构的首席法律顾问L.S.Leonard表示，该机构的评估结果显示，与澳大利亚采用的年龄验证方式相比，这种方法会“准确得多”。"},{"index":8,"en":"Yet things are not going to plan in Malaysia either. Mr Leonard says social‑media platforms claim to have removed lots of under‑age accounts, according to their own guidelines. But nothing has changed for most users, says Tricia Yeoh of the University of Nottingham’s Malaysian branch. Mr Leonard says platforms have asked for time to “make their system adaptable” for age verification; he expects everything “to be resolved” by January, after which non‑compliers may be fined. Ms Yeoh, however, suspects platforms are worried about the risks of storing personal IDs on systems that could be hacked, or subject to requests from governments.","zh":"然而，马来西亚的情况同样没有按计划发展。Leonard先生表示，根据社交媒体平台自己的规定，这些平台声称已经删除了大量未达到规定年龄的账号。但诺丁汉大学马来西亚分校的TriciaYeoh表示，对大多数用户来说，实际上什么都没有改变。Leonard先生说，各平台要求给予它们一些时间，以便“让系统适应”年龄验证；他预计这些问题将在明年1月前“得到解决”，届时仍不遵守规定的平台可能会被罚款。不过，Yeoh女士怀疑，各平台真正担心的是：如果把个人身份证明信息存储在可能遭到黑客入侵的系统中，或者这些信息可能被政府要求调取，就会带来相应的风险。"},{"index":9,"en":"Some oppose blunt social‑media bans like Australia’s because they think they let platforms get away with not making their sites safe. Ways to incentivise firms to do so are being contemplated. Canada plans to ban platforms from allowing under‑16s to have social‑media accounts, but only until these apps meet a set of safety criteria. And there are hopes that Meta, after introducing limits for teens in most American states, will roll the same features out elsewhere, and that other social‑media firms will follow suit.","zh":"一些人反对像澳大利亚这样“一刀切”的社交媒体禁令，因为他们认为这会反而让平台得以逃避责任，不去提升平台的安全性。目前，人们正在考虑通过各种方式激励企业采取这样的措施。加拿大计划禁止社交媒体平台允许16岁以下未成年人注册账号，但只有在这些应用达到一套规定的安全标准之前才会如此。与此同时，人们希望Meta在美国大多数州针对青少年推出相关限制措施后，也能将同样的功能推广到其他地区，并希望其他社交媒体公司也能纷纷效仿。"},{"index":10,"en":"Young Australians think they deserve more credit: Ms Naidu’s 14‑year‑old son says many teenagers already “know how to be safe online”. He stays off X, for example, because it is “very unfiltered”. He prefers Reddit, which is “less unhinged”.","zh":"澳大利亚的年轻人认为，他们应该得到更多认可。杜女士14岁的儿子说，许多青少年已经“知道如何安全地使用互联网”。比如，他不会使用X，因为那里“未经审查的内容太多”。相比之下，他更喜欢Reddit，因为那里“没那么失控”。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"curb","head":"v. To control or limit something, especially something undesirable; the edge of a street where the pavement meets the road.","definition":"To control or limit something, especially something undesirable; the edge of a street where the pavement meets the road.","gloss":"抑制；控制；路缘【考研大纲词汇】","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲 词汇"]},{"term":"tactic","head":"n. A particular method or plan used to achieve something, especially in a difficult situation.","definition":"A particular method or plan used to achieve something, especially in a difficult situation.","gloss":"策略；战术；手段","example":"The company changed its marketing tactics to attract younger customers.","exampleZh":"这家公司改变了营销策略，以吸引更年轻的顾客。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"underwhelming","head":"a. Not as impressive, exciting, or successful as expected.","definition":"Not as impressive, exciting, or successful as expected.","gloss":"不如预期的；令人失望的；平淡无奇的","example":"The results of the new policy were somewhat underwhelming. /v. /bæn/An official rule that prevents","exampleZh":"这项新政策的效果有些令人失望。","tags":["非考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"ban","head":"n. something from being done or used; to officially prohibit something.","definition":"something from being done or used; to officially prohibit something.","gloss":"禁令；禁止；取缔；禁止某事【考研大纲词汇】","example":"The government has imposed a ban on smoking in public places.","exampleZh":"政府已实施公共场所禁烟令。","tags":["考研 大纲词汇"]},{"term":"policymaker","head":"n. A person who is responsible for making or changing government policies.","definition":"A person who is responsible for making or changing government policies.","gloss":"政策制定者；决策者","example":"Policymakers must consider the long-term effects of the new policy.","exampleZh":"政策制定者必须考虑这项新政策的长期影响。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"Scrol","head":"v. skrəʊl/ To move text or images up or down on a screen; the act of moving through content on a screen.","definition":"skrəʊl/ To move text or images up or down on a screen; the act of moving through content on a screen.","gloss":"滚动；滚屏；浏览","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"lawsuit","head":"n. A legal case in which a person or organization seeks a decision from a court.","definition":"A legal case in which a person or organization seeks a decision from a court.","gloss":"诉讼；官司","example":"The company is facing a lawsuit over the safety of its products.","exampleZh":"这家公司正因其产品的安全问题面临诉讼。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"allege","head":"v. To say that someone has done something wrong or illegal without necessarily having proof.","definition":"To say that someone has done something wrong or illegal without necessarily having proof.","gloss":"声称；指控；宣称","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"youngster","head":"n. A young person, especially a child or teenager.","definition":"A young person, especially a child or teenager.","gloss":"年轻人；少年；儿童像伊莎娜这样的青少年的经历，对其他国家同样具有参考意义。自澳大利亚实施相关限制措施以来，已有数十个国家效仿或者正在考虑这样做。8 月 24 日，新西兰宣布计划实施禁令。政策制定者担心，社交媒体会对年轻人造成各种伤害。他们也知道，禁令很受成年人欢迎。8 月 26 日，当 Meta 同意在美国大多数州调整其面向 18 岁以下人群的产品后，许多成年人对此拍手叫好。调整措施包括将每天的刷屏时间限制在两小时以内。此前，Meta刚刚就一桩指控其平台伤害未成年人的诉讼达成和解。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"write off","head":"phrase. To decide that someone or something is unlikely to succeed or be useful, or to accept that something is lost or cannot be recovered.","definition":"To decide that someone or something is unlikely to succeed or be useful, or to accept that something is lost or cannot be recovered.","gloss":"认为……无用；认为……不会成功","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"migrate","head":"v. To move from one place to another, especially to live or work there; to move from one system or environment to another.","definition":"To move from one place to another, especially to live or work there; to move from one system or environment to another.","gloss":"迁移；移居；迁徙","example":"Many people migrate to cities in search of better job opportunities.","exampleZh":"许多人为了寻找更好的工作机会而迁往城市。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"alternative","head":"a. Something that can be used or done instead of another thing; different from the usual or traditional choice.","definition":"Something that can be used or done instead of another thing; different from the usual or traditional choice.","gloss":"替代方案；可供选择的事物；替代的","example":"Renewable energy provides an alternative to traditional sources of energy. 《","exampleZh":"可再生能源为传统能源提供了一种替代方案。然而，到目前为止，澳大利亚的这项政策基本上收效甚微。起初，政府还能够拿出一些成果来宣传。实施禁令后的第一个月，社交媒体平台就删除、限制使用或停用了近 500 万个账号。况且，现在断言澳大利亚新规没有效果或许还为时过早。但研究表明，到目前为止，这些规定对社交媒体使用情况的影响微乎其微。英国医学杂志》6 月发表的一项研究发现，在限制措施实施三个月后，85%的 16 岁以下青少年表示，他们仍在使用被禁的社交媒体平台。12 岁和 13 岁的孩子花在社交媒体上的时间与禁令实施前一样多。人们原本担心孩子会选择安全标准更低的其他媒体平台，但事实证明这种担忧大多没有成为现实——不过，这主要是因为许多的孩子仍然选择原有平台。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"outsmart","head":"v. /ˌaʊtˈsmɑː someone by using greater intelligence or better strategies.","definition":"/ˌaʊtˈsmɑː someone by using greater intelligence or better strategies.","gloss":"智胜；比……更聪明；智取 The player managed to outsmart his opponent with a clever strategy. 这名选手凭借巧妙的策略智胜了对手。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"joint","head":"a. /dʒɔɪnt/ A place where two things are connected; shared or done by two or more people or groups.","definition":"/dʒɔɪnt/ A place where two things are connected; shared or done by two or more people or groups.","gloss":"共同的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"confuse","head":"v. To make someone unable to understand something clearly; to mistake one person or thing for another.","definition":"To make someone unable to understand something clearly; to mistake one person or thing for another.","gloss":"使困惑；使混淆；把……弄错【考研大纲词汇】","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研 大纲词汇"]},{"term":"sibling","head":"n. A brother or sister.","definition":"A brother or sister.","gloss":"兄弟；姐妹；兄弟姐妹","example":"Children often learn how to share and cooperate with their siblings.","exampleZh":"孩子们常常从与兄弟姐妹相处中学会分享与合作。澳大利亚的年轻人仍然很想继续上网。伊莎娜说，一些未成年人甚至把这当成了一种挑战，因为 16 岁以下的孩子“反而因为社交媒体被禁止使用而更想用”。她解释说，年轻人“知道怎么钻系统的空子”，比如和朋友创建共同账号，她认为这种做法会让年龄验证系统难以判断。不过，她说，有几个使用真实出生日期注册的账号却没有被删除。许多 16 岁以下的孩子用虚假的年龄信息创建了新账号。还有一些人则填写了父母或兄弟姐妹的信息。","tags":[]},{"term":"verification","head":"n. The process of checking that something is true, accurate, or genuine.","definition":"The process of checking that something is true, accurate, or genuine.","gloss":"核实；验证；确认","example":"The information requires careful verification before it is published.","exampleZh":"这些信息在发布前需要仔细核实。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"commissioner","head":"n. An official who is responsible for a particular area or department, especially in government or an organization.","definition":"An official who is responsible for a particular area or department, especially in government or an organization.","gloss":"专员；委员；行政长官一些人将责任归咎于科技公司没有落实这些规定。软件测试公司 KJR 最近在澳大利亚开设了 50 个社交媒体账号，并声称这些账号的用户年龄均为 16 岁。该公司表示，只有一个网站进行了身份验证，而这 50 个账号全部仍处于正常使用状态。澳大利亚政府正试图进一步强化相关规定，其中包括将违规企业的罚款金额提高一倍，增至 9900 万澳元（约合 7100 万美元）。政府还希望赋予澳大利亚电子安全专员更大的权力，要求社交媒体公司提供其平台的内部使用数据。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"ineffectiveness","head":"n. The quality of not producing the intended result or effect.","definition":"The quality of not producing the intended result or effect.","gloss":"无效；不起作用；效果不佳","example":"The ineffectiveness of the policy has raised concerns among policymakers.","exampleZh":"这项政策的无效引发了政策制定者的担忧。","tags":[]},{"term":"scan","head":"v. skæn/ To look at something quickly and carefully in order to find particular information; a quick examination of something.","definition":"skæn/ To look at something quickly and carefully in order to find particular information; a quick examination of something.","gloss":"扫描；浏览；快速查看；扫描 检查 She scanned the report to find the information she needed. 她快速浏览了报告，以找到所需的信息。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"ID","head":"n. An identification document or number used to prove who someone is.","definition":"An identification document or number used to prove who someone is.","gloss":"身份证明；身份证件；身份识别号码","example":"You may be asked to show your ID when entering the building.","exampleZh":"进入大楼时，你可能会被要求出示身份证件。","tags":[]},{"term":"adaptable","head":"a. Able to change or adjust easily to different conditions or situations.","definition":"Able to change or adjust easily to different conditions or situations.","gloss":"适应性强的；能适应的；可调整的","example":"Young people are often more adaptable to changes in the workplace.","exampleZh":"年轻人通常更能适应工作环境中的变化。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"verification","head":"n. The process of checking that something is true, accurate, or genuine.","definition":"The process of checking that something is true, accurate, or genuine.","gloss":"核实；验证；确认","example":"The information requires careful verification before it is published.","exampleZh":"这些信息在发布前需要仔细核实。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"Hack","head":"v. hæk/ To gain unauthorized access to a computer or system; an act of gaining such access.","definition":"hæk/ To gain unauthorized access to a computer or system; an act of gaining such access.","gloss":"入 侵；非法侵入；黑客攻击；窍门 Hackers attempted to hack into the company's computer system. 黑客试图侵入该公司的计算机系统。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"blunt","head":"a. Not sharp or pointed; expressed in a direct way without trying to be polite; to make something less sharp or effective.","definition":"Not sharp or pointed; expressed in a direct way without trying to be polite; to make something less sharp or effective.","gloss":"直率的；直截了当的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"She was blunt about the problems with the current system.","exampleZh":"她直截了当地指出了现行制度存在的问题。","tags":["考 研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"incentivise","head":"v. To encourage someone to do something by offering them a reward or advantage.","definition":"To encourage someone to do something by offering them a reward or advantage.","gloss":"激励；鼓励；刺激","example":"The government introduced tax breaks to incentivise companies to invest in clean energy.","exampleZh":"政府推出税收优惠，以激励企业投资清洁能源。","tags":["非考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"contemplate","head":"v. To think carefully about something for a long time before making a decision.","definition":"To think carefully about something for a long time before making a decision.","gloss":"仔细考虑；深思；考虑","example":"The government is contemplating new measures to reduce carbon emissions.","exampleZh":"政府正在考虑采取新的措施来减少碳排放。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"follow suit","head":"phrase. To do the same thing as someone else, especially by following their example.","definition":"To do the same thing as someone else, especially by following their example.","gloss":"仿效；照着做；跟随……的做法","example":"Several other companies followed suit and introduced similar policies.","exampleZh":"其他几家公司也纷纷效仿，出台了类似的政策。","tags":[]},{"term":"unfiltered","head":"a. Not controlled, edited, or changed to remove unwanted or inappropriate content; expressed openly and directly.","definition":"Not controlled, edited, or changed to remove unwanted or inappropriate content; expressed openly and directly.","gloss":"未经过滤的；未经审查的；","example":"The interview gave viewers an unfiltered look at the athlete's life.","exampleZh":"这次采访让观众直接了解了这名运动员的生活。","tags":[]},{"term":"unhinged","head":"a. Behaving in an extremely strange, uncontrolled, or unreasonable way.","definition":"Behaving in an extremely strange, uncontrolled, or unreasonable way.","gloss":"失控的；不理智的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.10 检验题__阅读理解.docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"The family experience mentioned in Paragraph 1 functions in the text to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"show that Australia has successfully prevented teenagers from using virtual private networks"},{"key":"B","text":"suggest that parents generally prefer platform-designed safety features to legal restrictions"},{"key":"C","text":"illustrate that Australia's social-media ban has not changed many teenagers' actual access"},{"key":"D","text":"explain why social-media companies have deliberately delayed updating their age-checking systems"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·首段案例功能","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：But the rules, imposed in December, “literally did nothing”. Her son lost his YouTube account, but can still watch videos without logging in.","- 原文（Para.1）：Ishana was 15, but has kept her accounts on X, Instagram, Snapchat and TikTok... They do not even have to hide behind virtual private networks.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说他们甚至不需要借助 VPN，说明禁令没有有效阻止使用。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。首段只呈现家庭管理和禁令失效，没有比较家长对两类措施的偏好。","- 选项C（正确）：儿子可继续观看 YouTube，15 岁女儿仍保留多个平台账号，且无需 VPN。该案例具体说明禁令与实际使用之间有明显落差。","- 选项D（错误）：因果错位陷阱。平台年龄系统的问题在后文讨论，不是首段家庭案例要证明的观点。","【命题技巧】","- 例子与观点分层：Naidu 一家的经历服务于“禁令效果有限”这一全文引子。","- 细节反向核对：without logging in 与 kept her accounts 是排除 A 项的关键证据。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"The phrase “write off” (Paragraph 3) is closest in meaning to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"conclude that something has failed and is no longer worth serious consideration"},{"key":"B","text":"calculate the amount of a fine that a social-media company should pay"},{"key":"C","text":"permanently delete an under-age user's account from a platform's internal records"},{"key":"D","text":"postpone a final judgement until all policy data have been collected"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】词义猜测题·短语语境理解","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：And it may be too early to write off the effectiveness of Australia's new rules.","- 原文（Para.3）：But studies have shown they have so far had minimal impact on usage.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：前文承认政府曾宣传成绩，后文又指出效果甚微；too early to write off 即“现在就判定其失败/不再值得考虑为时尚早”。","- 选项B（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。罚款金额 A$99m 出现在后文第 5 段，与该短语语境无关。","- 选项C（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。write off 在这里不是平台删除账号的技术动作。","- 选项D（错误）：程度与语气偏差陷阱。短语强调“不要过早否定”，不是单纯推迟最终判断；且后文已有阶段性研究证据。","【命题技巧】","- 上下文情绪定位：successes、ineffective、minimal impact 共同限定 write off 的否定含义。","- 跨段词义排除：用后文罚款和账号信息制造似是而非的干扰。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 4 to 6 that the limited effect of Australia's ban partly stems from _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"official threats to double fines that have made platforms remove most under-age accounts"},{"key":"B","text":"children's large-scale migration to alternative platforms with lower safety standards"},{"key":"C","text":"face-scanning tools that consistently identify 15-year-olds as under the legal age"},{"key":"D","text":"young users' evasion tactics as well as the technical limits of age-verification systems"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·原因综合推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-6","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：Many under-16s have made new accounts using a fake age. Others have entered their parents' or siblings' details.","- 原文（Para.5）：KJR...opened 50 social-media accounts in Australia claiming the user to be 16. It said only one site did any verification and all 50 accounts remained active.","- 原文（Para.6）：But facial-age estimation software is not very accurate in distinguishing between, say, a 15- and 16-year-old... “The policy hasn’t been tested because it’s been technically impossible to enforce,” says Tama Leaver of Curtin University in Perth.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向因果陷阱。政府计划提高罚款，但 KJR 测试显示 50 个账号全部保持活跃，不能推出多数账号已被删除。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。第 3 段明确说儿童转向低标准替代平台的担忧 mostly unfounded，主要因为他们仍留在原平台。","- 选项C（错误）：细节反转陷阱。Lucina 的脸被 Snapchat 判断为 18 岁，说明系统可能高估年龄；原文还说该技术不够准确，并非持续识别为未满龄。","- 选项D（正确）：第 4 段讲青少年伪造年龄或使用家人信息，第 5-6 段讲平台核验不足和人脸年龄估计不准。两类因素共同推出执行困难。","【命题技巧】","- 双因归纳：用户策略与技术局限必须同时纳入，不能只取单一段落。","- 证据强度辨析：consistently、most 等绝对词与原文限定语冲突。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"Tricia Yeoh would most likely agree that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Malaysia's ID-based verification has already solved the country's enforcement problems"},{"key":"B","text":"platforms may be hesitant because storing personal IDs creates security and government-request risks"},{"key":"C","text":"Malaysia should replace official identity checks with Australia's facial-age estimation"},{"key":"D","text":"social-media firms have allowed independent regulators to audit all removed accounts"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】人物观点题·Tricia Yeoh 立场归属","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 8","【解析】","- 原文（Para.8）：But nothing has changed for most users, says Tricia Yeoh of the University of Nottingham's Malaysian branch.","- 原文（Para.8）：Ms Yeoh, however, suspects platforms are worried about the risks of storing personal IDs on systems that could be hacked, or subject to requests from governments.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。她说 nothing has changed for most users，说明问题尚未解决。","- 选项B（正确）：Yeoh suspects 平台担心个人 ID 可能被黑客攻击的系统存储，或面临政府调取请求。B 项保留 may be hesitant 的委婉推理，符合她的立场。","- 选项C（错误）：无中生有陷阱。她没有比较马来西亚 ID 制度与澳大利亚人脸年龄估计的优劣。","- 选项D（错误）：细节偷换陷阱。Leonard 说平台根据自身 guidelines 声称删除大量账号，不是允许独立监管者审计全部账号。","【命题技巧】","- 人物观点边界：Leonard 的官方说明与 Yeoh 的怀疑必须分开。","- 委婉语气保留：suspects/worried 对应 may be hesitant，避免过度确定。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Digital Natives Deserve More Credit: Teenagers Can Police Themselves Online"},{"key":"B","text":"Popular but Porous: Why Under-16 Social-Media Bans Are Hard to Enforce"},{"key":"C","text":"Platform Fines Fix Everything: A New Era of Age Assurance"},{"key":"D","text":"From Sydney to Kuala Lumpur: The End of Social Media Among Teenagers"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：Yet so far, Australia's policy has proved largely ineffective... studies have shown they have so far had minimal impact on usage.","- 原文（Para.6）：“The policy hasn’t been tested because it’s been technically impossible to enforce,” says Tama Leaver of Curtin University in Perth.","- 原文（Para.8）：Yet things are not going to plan in Malaysia either.","- 原文（Para.9）：Some oppose blunt social-media bans like Australia's because they think they let platforms get away with not making their sites safe.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。末段青少年的自我辩护只是补充声音，不是全文中心。","- 选项B（正确）：全文从澳大利亚个案扩展到多国政策，反复分析禁令受欢迎却难以有效执行：用户规避、平台核验不足、技术不准、马来西亚也遇挫。B 项同时概括政策吸引力和执行漏洞。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。罚款和数据调取只是政府尝试加强执行的手段，原文并未说它们能解决一切。","- 选项D（错误）：范围夸大陷阱。文章讨论禁令效果不彰，不是青少年社交媒体的终结。","【命题技巧】","- 地理案例串联：Australia、Malaysia、Canada 共同支撑政策执行难题。","- 标题限定词控制：Popular but porous 精准对应“政策受欢迎但漏洞明显”。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.10检验题__完型填空.docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["Yet so far, Australia’s policy has proved largely ineffective. At first the government was able to ____【11】____ some successes. Social-media platforms had removed, ____【12】____ or deactivated almost 5m accounts in the first month. And it may be too early to write ____【13】____ the effectiveness of Australia’s new rules. But studies have shown they have so far had minimal ____【14】____ on usage.","Young Aussies are keen to stay online. Some spy a challenge, says Ishana, as under-16s “want to use social media more because it’s banned”. The young “know how to ____【15】____ the system,” she explains, including by creating ____【16】____ accounts with friends, which she thinks confuses age-checking systems. Yet she says several accounts with her real date of birth were not ____【17】____. Many under-16s have made new accounts using a ____【18】____ age. Others have entered their parents’ or siblings’ details.","Some blame tech firms for not ____【19】____ the rules. KJR, a software-testing company, recently opened 50 social-media accounts in Australia claiming the user to be 16. It said only one site did any verification and all 50 accounts remained ____【20】____. The government is trying to beef up its rules, including by doubling fines on offending firms to A$99m ($71m)."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hide"},{"key":"B","text":"deny"},{"key":"C","text":"tout"},{"key":"D","text":"reject"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (tout)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·宣传语气","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] hide（隐藏）：政府最初想展示成果，不是隐藏。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] deny（否认）：否认成果与 able to 的能力语义不合。搭配干扰。","[C] tout（宣扬、吹嘘）：tout some successes 指政府宣传政策初步成果。正确答案。","[D] reject（拒绝）：拒绝成果与后文列举账号处理数量矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"restricted"},{"key":"B","text":"expanded"},{"key":"C","text":"ignored"},{"key":"D","text":"legalised"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (restricted)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·并列关系","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] restricted（限制）：与 removed、deactivated 并列，表示平台限制账号。正确答案。","[B] expanded（扩大）：方向与管控账号相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] ignored（忽视）：平台无法“忽视”账号后仍使账号受到处理。搭配干扰。","[D] legalised（使合法化）：与封禁政策语境相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"down"},{"key":"C","text":"up"},{"key":"D","text":"off"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (off)","analysis":["【题型】副词/小品词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第4句","【解析】","[A] on（继续）：write on 不表示“否定某事物的价值”。搭配干扰。","[B] down（写下）：write down 意为“写下”，不符合评价政策效果的语境。形近干扰。","[C] up（写满）：write up 指撰写报告，不能接 the effectiveness 的否定判断。搭配干扰。","[D] off（否定、认为不重要）：write off the effectiveness 意为“否定其效果”。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"benefit"},{"key":"B","text":"impact"},{"key":"C","text":"purpose"},{"key":"D","text":"opposition"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (impact)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·研究语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第5句","【解析】","[A] benefit（益处）：与 minimal 和后文青少年仍使用平台矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] impact（影响）：minimal impact on usage 指对使用量的影响很小。正确答案。","[C] purpose（目的）：研究评估的是效果，不是目的。语义场干扰。","[D] opposition（反对）：未涉及反对声音。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"obey"},{"key":"B","text":"abandon"},{"key":"C","text":"outsmart"},{"key":"D","text":"inspect"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (outsmart)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·语境语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] obey（遵守）：与因禁令而更想使用的心理相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] abandon（放弃）：与继续使用社交媒体的事实不符。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] outsmart（智取、巧妙绕过）：know how to outsmart the system 指年轻人懂得绕过系统限制。正确答案。","[D] inspect（检查）：年轻人不是检查系统。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"official"},{"key":"B","text":"joint"},{"key":"C","text":"private"},{"key":"D","text":"temporary"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (joint)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·方式语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] official（官方的）：朋友合用账号不是官方账号。语义场干扰。","[B] joint（共用的、联合的）：creating joint accounts with friends 指朋友共同使用账号。正确答案。","[C] private（私密的）：私密账号不能说明为何年龄核查被混淆。程度差异干扰。","[D] temporary（临时的）：强调时间长短而非多人共用。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"removed"},{"key":"B","text":"verified"},{"key":"C","text":"restored"},{"key":"D","text":"updated"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (removed)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·被动结果","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第4句","【解析】","[A] removed（移除）：real date of birth 的账号本应删除，但仍未被移除。正确答案。","[B] verified（核实）：语义可通，但与 were not 后的执行结果不如 removed 精确。近义干扰。","[C] restored（恢复）：不涉及恢复账号。语义场干扰。","[D] updated（更新）：不是更新信息的问题。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"real"},{"key":"B","text":"known"},{"key":"C","text":"fixed"},{"key":"D","text":"fake"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (fake)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·真假语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第5句","【解析】","[A] real（真实的）：真实年龄会触发封禁。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] known（已知的）：不能表达规避年龄核查的方式。语义场干扰。","[C] fixed（固定的）：fixed age 不表示虚假年龄。搭配干扰。","[D] fake（虚假的）：using a fake age 指使用虚假年龄注册。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"drafting"},{"key":"B","text":"reversing"},{"key":"C","text":"enforcing"},{"key":"D","text":"publicising"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (enforcing)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·法规语境","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] drafting（起草）：规则已经实施，不是尚未起草。时间关系干扰。","[B] reversing（撤销）：与后文罚款和加强规则矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] enforcing（执行）：not enforcing the rules 指科技公司未执行规定。正确答案。","[D] publicising（宣传）：问题不在宣传不足。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"closed"},{"key":"B","text":"active"},{"key":"C","text":"deleted"},{"key":"D","text":"suspended"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (active)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·状态语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] closed（关闭的）：与测试发现账号仍可使用相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] active（活跃的、有效的）：all 50 accounts remained active 表示账号仍处于可用状态。正确答案。","[C] deleted（已删除的）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] suspended（被暂停的）：与 remained 的可用状态矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.10精读.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":658994,"date":"2026-09-10","range":"","title":"Anti-social","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.10精读.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.10 检验题__阅读理解.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":56185,"date":"2026-09-10","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.10 检验题__阅读理解.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.10检验题__完型填空.docx","ext":".docx","bytes":59675,"date":"2026-09-10","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.10检验题__完型填空.docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"9.10杂志排版(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":700073,"date":"2026-09-10","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.10杂志排版(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
